    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49170" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θρῑνᾰκίη</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρῖναξ</span>) a legendary island, <i><span class="en">
			Od.
			11.107
		</span></i>, etc.: afterwards identified with Sicily and written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τρινακρία</span> (from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρεῖς, ἄκραι</span>) (q. v.); cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τριναχία</span>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θρῑνακίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, <i><span class="en">
			Str.
			6.2.1
		</span></i>:—Adj.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θρῑνάκιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<u>Sicilian</u>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥίζα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					529
				</span></i>
			.</div>
